{"path":"memory/unique_ptr/~unique_ptr","title":"std::unique_ptr<T,Deleter>::~unique_ptr","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::unique_ptr&lt;T,Deleter&gt;::</span>~unique_ptr","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/unique_ptr/~unique_ptr","section":"memory","kind":"page","summary":"If get() == nullptr there are no effects. Otherwise, the owned object is destroyed via get_deleter()(get()).","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">~unique_ptr<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> <br><span class=\"t-mark\">(constexpr since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>If <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/unique_ptr/get\">get()</a></span> <code>==</code> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">nullptr</span></code> there are no effects. Otherwise, the owned object is destroyed via <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/unique_ptr/get_deleter\">get_deleter()</a></span><code>(</code><span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/unique_ptr/get\">get()</a></span><code>)</code>.\n</p><p>Requires that <code>get_deleter()(get())</code> does not throw exceptions.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>Although <code>std::unique_ptr&lt;T&gt;</code> with the default deleter may be constructed with <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/type\">incomplete type</a> <code>T</code>, the type <code>T</code> must be complete at the point of code where the destructor is called.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\"><p>The following program demonstrates usage of a custom deleter.</p>\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;memory&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> \n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> deleter <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> ptr<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"[deleter called]<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        delete ptr<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/unique_ptr\"><span class=\"kw737\">std::<span class=\"me2\">unique_ptr</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span>, decltype<span class=\"br0\">(</span>deleter<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> uniq<span class=\"br0\">(</span>new <span class=\"kw4\">int</span>, deleter<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>uniq <span class=\"sy4\">?</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"not empty<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span> <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"empty<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    uniq.<span class=\"me1\">reset</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>uniq <span class=\"sy4\">?</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"not empty<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span> <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"empty<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>not empty\n[deleter called]\nempty</code></pre> \n</div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"memory","title":"Memory management library"},{"path":"memory/unique_ptr","title":"std::unique_ptr"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::unique_ptr<T,Deleter>::~unique_ptr","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++11. If get() == nullptr there are no effects. Otherwise, the owned object is destroyed via get_deleter()(get())."},{"label":"Notes","note":"Although std::unique_ptr<T> with the default deleter may be constructed with incomplete type T, the type T must be complete at the point of code where the…"},{"label":"Example","note":"The following program demonstrates usage of a custom deleter."}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":119,"codeBlockCount":2}
